The Vaquill Law Identifier specification, the registry, and the identifier
strings themselves are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal.

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

CC0 is a waiver, not a licence. Section 2 of the legal code has the Affirmer
"overtly, fully, permanently, irrevocably and unconditionally waive, abandon,
and surrender" the rights in the work. Surrendered rights cannot be reclaimed by
a later owner of the company, because there is nothing left to inherit. This is
deliberate and permanent.

The reference implementation in impl/ is licensed under the MIT License.
